{"title":"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has diameters <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> perpendicular to each other. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> is any chord intersecting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. \nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73a44cb7d629b6ef07c819ca0c8aedd0519bcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP\\cdot AM$\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> is equal to: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3da30e392e978e1b0205ac5cd8f006069965b7d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)); unitsize(2cm); pair O = origin; pair A = (-1,0); pair B = (1,0); pair C = (0,1); pair D = (0,-1); pair M = dir(45); pair P = intersectionpoint(O--C,A--M); draw(Circle(O,1)); draw(A--B); draw(C--D); draw(A--M); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,N); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,NE); label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,NE); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,NW);[/asy]\" width=\"238\" height=\"235\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/1/4d1550582e9bca8167787335c3283ae7991e551e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ AO\\cdot OB \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ AO\\cdot AB\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ CP\\cdot CD \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)}\\ CP\\cdot PD\\qquad  \\textbf{(E)}\\ CO\\cdot OP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"381\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856c130e0bb237c3edeb7e3c0246d40cc607e861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b6b3b3e9a6f7ded4fa2a6ff3256bdf75bd3f1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AMB$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is inscribed on a diameter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b6b3b3e9a6f7ded4fa2a6ff3256bdf75bd3f1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AMB$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AA_Similarity\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AA Similarity\">AA Similarity</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0c1a2dc986fd4e5b9c6cbb1de32970f213c380a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APO \\sim \\triangle ABM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />. Setting up ratios, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a1be34948ee3060f9c3fe95c13c33381968f05c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AP}{AO}=\\frac{AB}{AM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" />. Cross-multiplying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/6586c4b85bba8684e8ec114a9cad08c4c57ffc6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP\\cdot AM = AO \\cdot AB$\" width=\"167\" height=\"13\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Thales%27_Theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Thales&#39; Theorem\">Thales' Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/183430b425546182b288c8764a707afedadea16e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle PMB = \\measuredangle AMB = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"198\" height=\"15\" />. Because, from the problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da4dea1f8f069b4036732347607df9f35e55b0ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle POB = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" /> as well, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/9/ce985a96da4bf7f823297be302f089f263e572fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle PMB + \\measuredangle POB = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"201\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a0a6666d6168b916c78af08ec4c556d175fc63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PMBO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cyclic_quadrilateral\" title=\"Cyclic quadrilateral\">cyclic quadrilateral</a>. Thus, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lie on a circle, we can use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_of_a_Point\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Power of a Point\">Power of a Point</a>. From this theorem, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fbc61a9fd9434a74862de6fa0f74ec876a6b5ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP \\cdot AM = AO \\cdot AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"170\" height=\"14\" />, which is answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME\" title=\"1957 AHSME\">1957 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1957 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1957\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/